  "text": "Categories 6 Click a category to see its activity. Deleting one never deletes transactions. D Dining 3 transactions ✎ × F Fun 2 transactions ✎ × B Bills 1 transaction ✎ × F Food 1 transaction ✎ × I Income 0 transactions ✎ × U Uncategorized 3 transactions Let an AI make your categories Categories, rules and tags made for your own spending, with any AI chat you already use. The file holds only the names in your transactions (shops and payers), how often each one appears, and whether money went out or came in. It has no amounts, dates or accounts. It does leave the app: it goes to the AI company you choose. Download your transaction texts (12 different names). Download Copy the instructions, paste them into an AI chat (for example ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini), and attach the file. Copy instructions The AI answers with a file or a block of text. Upload it here to see what it would add. Upload the answer See the instructions I use a money app and want my spending sorted into categories. The attached file lists the names that appear in my transactions (shops and payers), how many times each appears, and whether money went out or came in. It also lists the categories and tags I already have. Please make: 1. categories: 8 to 25 clear categories that fit these transactions. Reuse my existing categories where they fit. Mark categories for money coming in with \"income\": true. Write the names in English, short and simple. 2. rules: for each name you can sort, a short piece of it (at least 2 letters) that always appears in it and does not appear in unrelated names, and the category it belongs to. One rule can cover many names, for example a chain with many branches. Every category used in a rule must be in your categories list or in mine. 3. tagRules: only if clearly useful, a short piece of a name and one or more tags (a short word, for example a trip or a project). Leave out names you are not sure about. I will sort those myself. Answer only with JSON in exactly this shape, with nothing before or after it: { \"categories\": [ { \"name\": \"Groceries\", \"income\": false }, { \"name\": \"Salary\", \"income\": true } ], \"rules\": [ { \"contains\": \"supermarket\", \"category\": \"Groceries\" } ], \"tagRules\": [ { \"contains\": \"hotel\", \"tags\": [ \"trip\" ] } ] } The AI gave text, not a file? Paste its whole answer here Check it",
